4.  nslookup Commands
   . nslookup example.com => Resolves the domain name example.com to its IP .  This command uses your system's default DNS server to resolve the domain name example.com to its IP address.
   . nslookup example.com 8.8.8.8 => Uses Google's DNS server (8.8.8.8) to resolve example.com. This command specifically queries Google's Public DNS server (8.8.8.8) to resolve the domain name example.com
   . nslookup -type=recordtype example.com => Replace recordtype with types such as A, MX, CNAME, TXT, etc., to view specific DNS records.


